# Meal Roulette — Cursor Rules

## Design Identity
This app blends three hand-drawn sketch styles on graph paper:
1. **Watercolor looseness** (Image ref 1) — warm washes, impressionistic fills, gestural color bleed
2. **Ink linework** (Image ref 2) — bold `2px` outlines, graphic black borders, confident strokes
3. **Annotated food journal** (Image ref 3) — ingredient callouts with arrows, handwritten labels, scrapbook density

The result is a tactile food diary. Every screen should feel like a sketched notebook page. Never clean, never corporate.

---

## Fonts
Always import and use:
- **Kalam** (700) — display text, headings, recipe titles, CTAs, section labels
- **Caveat** (400, 600, 700) — body text, annotations, tags, metadata, journal notes

```html
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Caveat:wght@400;600;700&family=Kalam:wght@300;400;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
```

Never use Inter, Roboto, Arial, or any system font. Ever.

---

## Colors
Use only these — all named after food ingredients:

```
--chili:     #c0392b   /* primary action, borders, tags, highlights */
--herb:      #3a6644   /* cuisine labels, success states, checkmarks */
--saffron:   #d4813a   /* watercolor wash accents, card top bands */
--turmeric:  #b8973a   /* secondary decorative accents */
--miso:      #7a4f2a   /* deep accents, dark element borders */
--ink:       #2b2118   /* ALL outlines, headings, structural text */
--paper:     #f7f2e8   /* backgrounds, card fills */
--grid:      #c9dce8   /* graph paper lines, notebook rule lines */
--margin:    #e8a090   /* notebook margin lines */
--muted:     #9a856a   /* section labels, secondary text, annotations */
```

