## Background
Every page and full-width container uses graph paper:

```css
background-color: #f7f2e8;
background-image:
  linear-gradient(#c9dce8 1px, transparent 1px),
  linear-gradient(90deg, #c9dce8 1px, transparent 1px);
background-size: 24px 24px;
```

---

## Borders
- All borders: `2px solid #2b2118` — thick ink lines
- No border-radius anywhere on cards, buttons, tags, or inputs (0 = hand-drawn feel)
- Section dividers: `1.5px dashed #c8b89a`
- Subtle double-outline on cards: add a `::after` at `bottom: -3px; right: -3px; left: 3px; top: 3px; border: 1.5px solid #2b2118; opacity: 0.2`

---

## Card Rotation
All cards, swatches, and decorative blocks are slightly rotated:
- Recipe cards: `transform: rotate(0.9deg)`
- Preference cards: `transform: rotate(-0.7deg)`
- Buttons: `transform: rotate(-1.2deg)`
- Swatches / decorative blocks: `rotate(±0.5deg to ±1.5deg)`

---

## Offset Shadow (NEVER use box-shadow)
Use a `::before` pseudo-element for all shadows:

```css
.element {
  position: relative;
}
.element::before {
  content: '';
  position: absolute;
  bottom: -5px;
  right: -5px;
  left: 5px;
  top: 5px;
  background: #c0392b;   /* or #2b2118 for secondary */
  opacity: 0.7;
  z-index: -1;
}
```

Lighter variant (for small UI elements): shift `3px`, `opacity: 0.15`.

---

## Watercolor Wash (inspired by Image 1)
Simulate watercolor fill using flat color with opacity — never CSS gradients:

```css
/* Top band on recipe cards */
.card-wash {
  position: absolute;
  top: 0; left: 0; right: 0;
  height: 5px;
  background: #d4813a;
  opacity: 0.6;
}

/* Color fill on wheel segments */
fill="#d4813a" opacity="0.85"
```

Color bleeds and washes = flat fill + opacity. Not gradients.

---

## Annotation Style (inspired by Image 3)
Add ingredient/detail callouts using italic Caveat with arrow characters:

```css
.annotation {
  font-family: 'Caveat', cursive;
  font-size: 13px;
  font-style: italic;
  color: #7a6249;
}
```

Used as: `← deep-fried tofu, slightly crispy` or `→ substitute with tempeh`
Place near relevant elements. This is a core UI pattern, not decoration.

---

## Notebook Lines (inspired by Images 2 & 3)
For preference cards, journal blocks, and note areas:

```css
background-image: repeating-linear-gradient(
  transparent,
  transparent 27px,
  #c9dce8 27px,
  #c9dce8 28px
);
```

Add red margin line:
```css
.margin-line {
  position: absolute;
  left: 38px; top: 0; bottom: 0;
  border-left: 1.5px solid #e8a090;
}
```
Content indented `50–52px` from left to clear the margin.

